  "Question": "If \\(2\\) is a solution (root) of \\(x^3+hx+10=0,\\) then \\(h\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(10\\)",
    "B": "\\(9\\)",
    "C": "\\(2\\)",
    "D": "\\(-2\\)",
    "E": "\\(-9\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Because \\(2\\) is a root, substituting \\(x=2\\) must make the left side zero. This gives a linear equation in \\(h\\):\n\\[\n2^3+2h+10=0,\n\\qquad 2h=-18.\n\\]\nDividing by \\(2\\) yields \\(h=\\boxed{-9}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
